  "body": "## What changed\n\nDeburr now generates in an aligned milling setup.\nThe supported-kind refusal message names Deburr.\nThree existing refusal tests use Probe, which remains unsupported.\nThe decision record explains the world-read audit.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe verified-kind list omitted Deburr.\nIts material, model bounds, model-relative heights and part protection already read the setup frame.\nThe Deburr kernel consumes those facets without reading the world.\nStock and fixtures stay in the setup frame.\n\n## Tests\n\n`turned_deburr_cuts_like_the_baked_part` covers a whole-model source.\n`turned_selected_deburr_cuts_like_the_baked_part` covers a selected-face source.\nBoth pins failed on unchanged upstream/main b4be144f6 with the aligned-setup refusal.\nBoth pass with this fix.\nThey compare a two-axis turned setup with the same turn baked into the mesh.\nThey require equal toolpaths and exactly equal posted programs.\nThey check model-relative heights, the analytic turned top rim and simulation without gouges.\nThe part as modelled must cut differently or refuse.\n\nRestoring upstream/main's old setup_align.rs made both pins fail.\nRestoring the fix made both pass.\nSeparate mutations to model-frame material facets and model-frame heights each made both pins fail.\nRestoring each reader made both pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all 15 steps on the final tree.\nThe gate ran 14 suites with 453 passed, one ignored and zero failed.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\nThe first gate exposed obsolete refusal tests, which this PR updates.\nClippy also caught the single-element loop left by removing Deburr, which this PR flattens.\nThe shared compiler cache stalled, so verification ran with its wrapper unset and automatic cache setup disabled.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo machine or controller run was performed.\nThe proof uses the shipped 90-degree chamfer mill and a two-axis quarter-turn L prism.\nThe release gate and GUI were not exercised.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR changes any touched file.\nThis branch starts at upstream/main b4be144f6.\n\nChangelog: Deburr supports aligned milling setups with proven setup-frame geometry and model-relative heights.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2284\n",
